  "text": "How to set strict revision boundaries without upsetting high-paying clients. Unlimited revision requests secretly eat away your agency profits until you are working for minimum wage. Vague contract clauses fail because clients expect endless micro-tweaks unless the submission system physically restricts them. Build a Notion client hub that limits revisions to two rounds and automatically invoices extra requests. You eliminate costly scope creep while maintaining sixty percent margins.",
